       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the labeled maximum for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day under prescription labeling. The OTC limit is 1,200 mg/day. A dose that high raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events.\n\nHere are some options that stay within the limit:\n- **800 mg by mouth four times daily** (3,200 mg/day). This is the maximum daily dose.\n- **600 mg by mouth four times daily** (2,400 mg/day). This is a common dose for pain or inflammation.\n- **400 mg by mouth every 6 hours** (1,600 mg/day) for milder pain.\n\nMaybe you meant 1600 mg total per day, or 400 mg four times daily. Tell me which dose you want, and I'll enter it right away. If the aim is stronger pain control, I can also enter a multimodal regimen, such as scheduled acetaminophen alongside ibuprofen."
